# Normalise line endings.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default. A shell script that
# reaches a Linux container with CRLF fails as "no such file or directory",
# because the kernel reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r" and looks for a
# program of that name. CI checks out on Linux and never sees it, so without
# this the Docker build works everywhere except a Windows developer's machine.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
